"I offer neither pay, nor quarters, nor food;
I offer only hunger, thirst, forced marches, battles and death.
Let him who loves his country with his heart, and not merely with his lips, follow me."

My people sleep a deep and lifeless sleep; 
no parent's hand to wipe away my tears.
Above my head the heaven is shut tight;
it does not hear my cries or my prayers.

–Petar II Petrović-Njegoš, The Mountain Wreath

The great steel vessel steamed forth into the port, flying not its given … flag, but rather that of …. Sailors on the deck cheered as they made ready to flee into the bowels of its new home city, free at last from the horrors of maggoted rations and rusting berths.

And as the poor people of … beheld the pursuit craft begin their chase of the …, a thought crossed their minds;

"We won't forget!"
